IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rawq-dates`
IMPORT `rawq-commencement`
IMPORT `rawq-claimant`

-- Respect at Work and Other Matters Amendment Act 2024 (Queensland) -- worked cases for the complainant's questions
-- (rawq-claimant.l4), the commencement rules (rawq-commencement.l4) and the date helper (rawq-dates.l4). Every expected
-- value was worked by hand from the deposited text (and, for "what the 1991 Act shows", from the deposited Anti-
-- Discrimination Act 1991); none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on
-- stated facts, not about the law.
--
-- The 1 July 2025 group had not commenced on the deposited evidence. Cases use three settings for it: not commenced
-- (`not yet`, with an unused day); commenced on 1 July 2025 as s 2(2) passed it (`as passed`); and commenced on
-- 1 March 2027, an invented day (`later`) standing for a deferred commencement. None of these says what later
-- legislation actually did.
--
-- Day counts used: 1 year after 14 March 2025 is 14 March 2026; 1 year after 1 July 2024 is 1 July 2025 (not before
-- 1 July 2025, so not "more than 1 year before" it); 1 year after 30 June 2024 is 30 June 2025 (before 1 July 2025);
-- 2 years after 1 July 2024 is 1 July 2026; 1 year after 1 January 2026 is 1 January 2027 (before 1 March 2027);
-- 1 year after 1 April 2026 is 1 April 2027 (not before 1 March 2027), 2 years after it 1 April 2028; 1 year after
-- 29 February 2024 is 28 February 2025 (fork F10), 2 years after it 28 February 2026.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`unused` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000
`as passed day` MEANS `d` 1 7 2025
`later day` MEANS `d` 1 3 2027

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 2 -- when each change commences, and its status`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`Dec` MEANS `on 1 December 2024 (s 2(1))`
`Jul` MEANS `on 1 July 2025 (s 2(2))`
`ART` MEANS `immediately after the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth) s 8 commences (s 2(3)); that day is not in the deposited sources`
`unnamed` MEANS `s 2 does not name it: its commencement is left to the Acts Interpretation Act 1954, which is not deposited`

`p s29` MEANS `s 29 (the 2-year complaint period, s 138)`
`p s31` MEANS `s 31 (representative complaints to the commissioner, new ss 146 to 152A)`
`p s47A` MEANS `s 47A (burden of proof, new ss 204 and 205)`
`p s1-2` MEANS `ss 1 and 2 (short title and commencement)`
`p pt11` MEANS `part 11 and schedule 2 (amendments for the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth))`
`p pt6` MEANS `part 6 (Human Rights Act 2019)`
`p s3` MEANS `part 2 heading and s 3 (Act amended)`
`p s52(3)` MEANS `s 52(3) (definition complainant)`
`p sch1` MEANS `schedule 1 (other amendments of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991)`
`p cc` MEANS `ss 56 to 59 (Criminal Code vilification offences)`
`p cc other` MEANS `part 4 heading, s 55 and s 59A (other Criminal Code amendments)`
`p courts` MEANS `parts 5, 6A, 7, 8, 9, 9A and 10 (courts, judges and sentencing)`
`p trans other` MEANS `s 51 so far as it inserts ss 283, 284, 285A, 286 and 287 (the other transitional provisions)`
`p trans 285` MEANS `s 51 so far as it inserts ss 282 and 285 (transitional definitions; existing representative complaints)`
`p s18` MEANS `s 18 (harassment on the basis of sex, chapter 3 part 3)`
`p s7B` MEANS `s 7B (new meanings of direct and indirect discrimination, ss 10, 11 and 11A)`
`p s28(1)` MEANS `s 28(1) (note to s 134(1) on representative complaints)`
`p s28(2)` MEANS `s 28(2) to (6) (who may act as my agent, s 134(2), and the other changes to s 134)`

-- s 2(1)(b) "sections 3, 28(1), 31, 37, 38 and 46 to 48"; s 47A within "46 to 48" (fork F1).
