`st dec in` MEANS `commenced on 1 December 2024 under s 2(1), and the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 contains it`
`st dec none` MEANS `commenced on 1 December 2024 under s 2(1); it changes no text of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991`
`st deferred` MEANS `due on 1 July 2025 under s 2(2) as passed, but the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 in force on 6 November 2026 does not contain it: later legislation, not deposited here, has deferred or changed its commencement`
`st jul other Act` MEANS `due on 1 July 2025 under s 2(2) as passed; it amends another Act, not checked here`
`st ART` MEANS `commences immediately after the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cwlth) s 8 commences (s 2(3)); that day is not in the deposited sources`
`st unnamed` MEANS `not named in s 2: its commencement is left to the Acts Interpretation Act 1954, which is not deposited`

-- Read from the deposited Anti-Discrimination Act 1991: s 146(2), ss 194 to 203A and new ss 204, 205 are there; s 138
-- still says 1 year; there is no chapter 3 part 3; s 10 still says "less favourably"; s 285AA stands in place of
-- ss 283 to 287; schedule 1's "unfavourably" wording is unchanged.
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s31` EQUALS `st dec in`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s47A` EQUALS `st dec in`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s28(1)` EQUALS `st dec in`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s3` EQUALS `st dec none`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s29` EQUALS `st deferred`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s18` EQUALS `st deferred`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s7B` EQUALS `st deferred`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s28(2)` EQUALS `st deferred`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p trans other` EQUALS `st deferred`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p sch1` EQUALS `st deferred`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p pt6` EQUALS `st jul other Act`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p cc` EQUALS `st jul other Act`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p pt11` EQUALS `st ART`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p courts` EQUALS `st unnamed`
#ASSERT `What is the commencement status of this change` `p s1-2` EQUALS `st unnamed`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 7 -- attributes`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`attr old` MEANS `yes: it is an attribute in s 7, before and after the amending Act`
`attr new in` MEANS `yes: the amending Act added it to s 7, and that change was in force when the conduct happened`
`attr new out` MEANS `no: the amending Act adds it to s 7, but that change was not in force when the conduct happened`
`attr none` MEANS `no: it is not an attribute set out in s 7 (schedule 1, attribute)`
`race new in` MEANS `yes: the amending Act named it in the definition of race, and that change was in force when the conduct happened`
`race new out` MEANS `not covered: the amending Act names it in the definition of race, but that change was not in force when the conduct happened, and the former definition ("race includes" colour, descent or ancestry, ethnicity or ethnic origin, nationality or national origin) neither names nor excludes it`

#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `sex` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `attr old`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `sexual orientation (formerly sexuality)` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `attr old`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `family responsibilities` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `attr old`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `association with, or relation to, a person with any of these attributes` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `attr old`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `homelessness` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `attr new out`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `homelessness` (`d` 28 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `attr new out`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `homelessness` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `attr new in`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `carer or kinship responsibilities, beyond responsibilities to my family` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `attr new in`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `potential pregnancy (being able to, wanting to or being likely to become pregnant, or fertility treatment)` (`d` 30 6 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `attr new out`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `a combination of 2 or more of these attributes` (`d` 1 7 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `attr new in`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `an irrelevant medical record (including workers compensation claims)` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `attr new out`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `something not in this list` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `attr none`
-- Race: the former heads throughout; caste and immigration or migration status only from the 1 July 2025 group, and
-- "not covered" before it, since the former "race includes" does not close its list (fork F16).
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `race, as colour, descent or ancestry, ethnicity or ethnic origin, or nationality or national origin` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `attr old`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `race, as colour, descent or ancestry, ethnicity or ethnic origin, or nationality or national origin` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `attr old`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `race, as caste or immigration or migration status` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `race new out`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `race, as caste or immigration or migration status` (`d` 28 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `race new out`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `race, as caste or immigration or migration status` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `race new in`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `race, as caste or immigration or migration status` (`d` 30 6 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `race new out`
#ASSERT `Is my attribute protected` `race, as caste or immigration or migration status` (`d` 1 7 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `race new in`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ch 3 pt 3 -- harassment on the basis of sex`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`co-workers` MEANS `we are workers in the same business or undertaking`
`not in force h` MEANS `no: chapter 3 part 3 was not in force when the conduct happened`
`not s 120` MEANS `no: the conduct does not meet s 120 (it must be unwelcome and demeaning, on the basis of sex, and intended to offend, humiliate or intimidate or such that a reasonable person would have anticipated that)`
`no prohibition` MEANS `not covered: it meets s 120, but chapter 3 part 3 has no prohibition for how you stand to the person (other provisions may still apply, s 120AA)`
`prohibited by` MEANS `yes: harassment on the basis of sex (s 120), prohibited by the section named`

#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `my sex` TRUE FALSE `co-workers` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `prohibited by` "s 120B(a)"
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `my sex` TRUE FALSE `co-workers` (`d` 28 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `not in force h`
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `my sex` TRUE FALSE `co-workers` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `not in force h`
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` FALSE TRUE `my sex` TRUE TRUE `co-workers` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `not s 120`
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE FALSE `my sex` TRUE TRUE `co-workers` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `not s 120`
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `none of these` TRUE TRUE `co-workers` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `not s 120`
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `a characteristic often imputed to people of my sex` FALSE TRUE `co-workers` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `prohibited by` "s 120B(a)"
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `my sex` FALSE FALSE `co-workers` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `not s 120`
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `my sex` TRUE TRUE `none of these` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `no prohibition`
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `a sex I have been, though I am not that sex now` TRUE TRUE `they have power to grant, renew or extend a professional, trade or business qualification or authorisation I seek` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `prohibited by` "s 120E"
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `my sex` TRUE TRUE `I conduct a business or undertaking, or work in one` (`d` 1 7 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `prohibited by` "s 120C"
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `my sex` TRUE TRUE `they conduct a business or undertaking in which I work or seek work` (`d` 1 7 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `prohibited by` "s 120A(a), (b)"
#ASSERT `Was it harassment on the basis of sex` TRUE TRUE `my sex` TRUE TRUE `I am seeking membership of an organisation of which they are a member` (`d` 1 7 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `prohibited by` "s 120D(b)"

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 124E -- hostile work environment`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`hostile yes` MEANS `yes: you were subjected to a work environment hostile on the basis of sex, which s 124E(1) prohibits`
`hostile no` MEANS `no: the conduct does not meet s 124E(2)`
`hostile not in force` MEANS `no: s 124E was not in force when the conduct happened`

#ASSERT `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `hostile yes`
#ASSERT `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `hostile no`
#ASSERT `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `hostile no`
#ASSERT `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `hostile no`
#ASSERT `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 28 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `hostile not in force`
#ASSERT `Was I subjected to a hostile work environment` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `hostile not in force`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ch 5C -- the positive duty`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`duty yes` MEANS `yes: they must take reasonable and proportionate measures to eliminate discrimination and harassment as far as possible (s 131I(3)); you cannot complain of a breach yourself, but the commissioner may investigate and enforce it (chapter 7 part 1A)`
`duty no individual` MEANS `no: an individual owes the duty only if they conduct a business or undertaking (s 131I(2))`
`duty outside` MEANS `not covered: they are not under a chapter 2, 3, 4 or 5 prohibition towards people like you (s 131I(1))`
`duty not in force` MEANS `no: chapter 5C was not in force on that day`

#ASSERT `Does the positive duty protect me` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `duty yes`
#ASSERT `Does the positive duty protect me` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `duty no individual`
#ASSERT `Does the positive duty protect me` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `duty yes`
#ASSERT `Does the positive duty protect me` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `duty outside`
#ASSERT `Does the positive duty protect me` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 28 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `duty not in force`
#ASSERT `Does the positive duty protect me` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `duty not in force`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 138, 283 -- time limits`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`in time former` MEANS `yes, in time under former s 138(1): within 1 year after the alleged contravention`
`in time new` MEANS `yes, in time under new s 138(1): within the 2-year complaint period`
`out of time` MEANS `no, out of time: the commissioner must not accept the complaint unless satisfied you have shown good cause (s 138(2)); s 141A may let the commissioner defer that decision where other contraventions in the complaint are in time`

-- Not commenced: 1 year, the last day 14 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 14 3 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `in time former`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `out of time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `in time former`
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 14 3 2026
-- Commenced on 1 July 2025 (as passed). 1 July 2024 is not more than 1 year before: 2 years, the last day 1 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 1 7 2024) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `d` 1 7 2026
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 1 7 2026) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `in time new`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 7 2024) (`d` 2 7 2026) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `out of time`
-- 30 June 2024 is more than 1 year before: s 283 keeps 1 year, the last day 30 June 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 30 6 2024) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `d` 30 6 2025
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 30 6 2024) (`d` 30 6 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `in time former`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 30 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS `out of time`
-- Commenced on the invented day 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `d` 1 1 2027
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `out of time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `out of time`
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 1 4 2026) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `d` 1 4 2028
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 4 2026) (`d` 31 3 2028) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `in time new`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 4 2026) (`d` 2 4 2028) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `out of time`
-- A complaint made before the commencement meets the former s 138, though the new one would allow longer.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 4 2026) (`d` 1 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `in time former`
-- "By when" gives the new last day whenever the new s 138 reaches the contravention; a complaint made before the
-- commencement is then always within the former 1 year too, because the anniversary is on or after the commencement
-- (s 283). The edge: contravention 1 March 2026, exactly 1 year before the commencement on 1 March 2027 (not "more
-- than"): the last day is 1 March 2028; a complaint on 28 February 2027 (before commencement) is in time under the
-- former s 138; one on 1 March 2028 under the new.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `d` 1 3 2028
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 28 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `in time former`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2028) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `in time new`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 2 3 2028) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `out of time`
-- 29 February.
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 29 2 2024) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `out of time`
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 28 2 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
-- A complaint dated before the contravention (fork F11).
#ASSERT `Am I in time to complain` (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 31 12 2025) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `in time former`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 134(2), 284 -- agents`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`unregistered` MEANS `an employee or officer of, or a person acting for, an unregistered body that claims to represent the industrial interests of employees or employers`
`registered org` MEANS `an employee or officer of, or a person acting for, a registered organisation (a union or employer body registered under the Industrial Relations Act 2016 or the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act 2009)`
`lawyer` MEANS `a person not connected with a body that represents industrial interests (for example a lawyer, relative or advocate)`
`agent yes` MEANS `yes: an agent may complain for you (s 134(1)(b))`
`agent no` MEANS `no: for a work-related complaint, your agent cannot be from a body other than a registered organisation that claims to represent industrial interests (s 134(2))`

#ASSERT `Can this person complain for me as my agent` `unregistered` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `agent no`
#ASSERT `Can this person complain for me as my agent` `unregistered` TRUE (`d` 28 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `agent yes`
#ASSERT `Can this person complain for me as my agent` `unregistered` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `agent yes`
#ASSERT `Can this person complain for me as my agent` `registered org` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `agent yes`
#ASSERT `Can this person complain for me as my agent` `lawyer` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `agent yes`
#ASSERT `Can this person complain for me as my agent` `unregistered` TRUE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `agent yes`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 146, 148, 149, 195, 209, 285 -- representative complaints`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`old law` MEANS `the former chapter 7, parts 1 and 2 continue to govern it, as if the amending Act had not been enacted (s 285(2)); the commissioner or tribunal may still give directions to bring it into line with the new law (s 285(3))`
`new law` MEANS `the new law governs it (the amending Act, ss 31, 37, 38, 46 to 48, from 1 December 2024)`

#ASSERT `Which law governs the representative complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `old law`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the representative complaint` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `new law`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the representative complaint` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `new law`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the representative complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `new law`

#ASSERT `Can I make a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Outside the class, or not a registered employee organisation: outside the grant's own wording, NOTHING (fork F18).
#ASSERT `Can I make a representative complaint` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I make a representative complaint` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Can my union make a representative complaint for us` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my union make a representative complaint for us` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my union make a representative complaint for us` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my union make a representative complaint for us` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my union make a representative complaint for us` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my union make a representative complaint for us` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2024) EQUALS NOTHING

`going ahead` MEANS `nothing of these: it is going ahead as a representative complaint`
`own not member` MEANS `yes: you are not a member of the class, so the representative complaint does not prevent you (s 149(1), s 196(1))`
`own opted out` MEANS `yes: you opted out, so the representative complaint does not prevent you (s 149(2), s 196(2))`
`own released` MEANS `yes: the bar on a separate complaint does not apply to you, because of what has happened to the representative complaint (s 148(2) or (3))`
`own barred` MEANS `no: as a member of the class you are not entitled to make a separate complaint about the same conduct unless you opt out (s 148(1)(b), s 195(1)(b))`
`own former` MEANS `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including whether you may complain separately`

#ASSERT `Can I make my own complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE `going ahead` FALSE EQUALS `own not member`
#ASSERT `Can I make my own complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE `going ahead` FALSE EQUALS `own opted out`
#ASSERT `Can I make my own complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE `going ahead` FALSE EQUALS `own barred`
#ASSERT `Can I make my own complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE `after referral to the tribunal, it lapsed (s 193)` FALSE EQUALS `own released`
#ASSERT `Can I make my own complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the commissioner amended it to be a non-representative complaint (s 151)` FALSE EQUALS `own released`
#ASSERT `Can I make my own complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the tribunal ordered it no longer continue as a representative complaint (s 198 or s 199)` FALSE EQUALS `own released`
#ASSERT `Can I make my own complaint` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the commissioner amended it to be a non-representative complaint (s 151)` FALSE EQUALS `own barred`
#ASSERT `Can I make my own complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE `going ahead` TRUE EQUALS `own former`

`opt commissioner yes` MEANS `yes: you may opt out by written notice to the commissioner before the commissioner finally deals with the complaint (s 148(1)(a))`
`opt commissioner no` MEANS `no: the commissioner has finally dealt with the complaint`
`opt tribunal yes` MEANS `yes: you may opt out by written notice to the tribunal before the opt-out date it fixed (s 195(1)(a))`
`opt tribunal no` MEANS `no: the opt-out date the tribunal fixed has come (s 195(1)(a)); the tribunal may fix a later one on application (s 195(4))`
`opt former` MEANS `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including opting out`

#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the representative complaint` `with the commissioner` FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `opt commissioner yes`
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the representative complaint` `with the commissioner` TRUE `unused` (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `opt commissioner no`
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the representative complaint` `referred to the tribunal` FALSE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 31 5 2026) FALSE EQUALS `opt tribunal yes`
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the representative complaint` `referred to the tribunal` FALSE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `opt tribunal no`
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the representative complaint` `with the commissioner` FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS `opt former`

`costs yes` MEANS `yes: in a representative complaint the tribunal may order costs against the complainant or the respondent (s 209(5)(a))`
`costs no` MEANS `no: in a representative complaint costs may not be ordered against a class member other than the complainant (s 209(5)(a))`
`costs tribunal Act` MEANS `not covered: outside a representative complaint, costs are as the relevant tribunal Act provides (s 209(5)(b)), which is not encoded here`
`costs former` MEANS `not covered: the former law governs this representative complaint (s 285), including costs`

#ASSERT `Can costs be ordered against me` TRUE `the complainant` FALSE EQUALS `costs yes`
#ASSERT `Can costs be ordered against me` TRUE `a class member, not the complainant` FALSE EQUALS `costs no`
#ASSERT `Can costs be ordered against me` TRUE `the respondent` FALSE EQUALS `costs yes`
#ASSERT `Can costs be ordered against me` FALSE `the complainant` FALSE EQUALS `costs tribunal Act`
#ASSERT `Can costs be ordered against me` TRUE `a class member, not the complainant` TRUE EQUALS `costs former`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 204, 205, 285A, 285AA -- burden of proof`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`burden new` MEANS `new s 204: if there are facts from which it could be decided, in the absence of any other explanation, that the respondent contravened the Act, the respondent is taken to have done so unless it proves on the balance of probabilities that it did not; a respondent relying on an exemption must prove it applies (s 205)`
`burden former` MEANS `former ss 204 to 206 continue to apply to your complaint (s 285AA of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991; s 285A of the amending Act as passed); their text is not deposited here`

#ASSERT `Who must prove what in my complaint` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `burden former`
#ASSERT `Who must prove what in my complaint` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 2 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `burden new`
#ASSERT `Who must prove what in my complaint` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `burden new`
#ASSERT `Who must prove what in my complaint` (`d` 28 2 2027) (`d` 2 3 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `burden former`
#ASSERT `Who must prove what in my complaint` (`d` 1 2 2027) (`d` 15 2 2027) TRUE `later day` EQUALS `burden former`

-- The amending Act alone, as passed (finding 3): new ss 204, 205 from 1 December 2024 with no transitional rule until
-- the 1 July 2025 group commences. The same facts as the first case above give the new burden, where s 285AA now
-- gives the former.
#ASSERT `ss 204, 205, 285A -- new burden of proof under the Act as passed` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE `unused` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 204, 205, 285A -- new burden of proof under the Act as passed` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 2 2024) (`d` 30 11 2024) FALSE `unused` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 204, 205, 285A -- new burden of proof under the Act as passed` (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) (`d` 1 8 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 204, 205, 285A -- new burden of proof under the Act as passed` (`d` 1 7 2025) (`d` 2 7 2025) (`d` 1 8 2025) TRUE `as passed day` EQUALS TRUE
